WEBVTT

00:05.600 --> 00:10.110
I forgot we changed seats 
and just tried to sit in my old one!

00:10.110 --> 00:11.960
El-oh-el!

00:11.960 --> 00:15.340
But nice job, Nicole. 
You're basically in the same spot.

00:15.340 --> 00:18.830
Akari, don't underestimate my luck.

00:37.900 --> 00:43.480
If we can, will you become 
Maria's friend with me?

00:43.800 --> 00:46.720
<i>It looks like the "Become Friends 
with Kurose-san Project"</i>

00:46.720 --> 00:50.190
<i>hasn't found a way to take off yet.</i>

00:50.770 --> 00:51.780
<i>Meanwhile...</i>

00:52.150 --> 00:55.110
I spent the whole summer watching videos.

00:55.110 --> 00:57.820
That's how it goes for geeks like us.

00:57.820 --> 00:59.830
Unlike this other guy here.

00:59.830 --> 01:03.290
I was thinking... Are you free this Saturday?

01:03.290 --> 01:04.750
<b><i>Apple Juice</i></b>

01:03.680 --> 01:04.750
Hah?

01:05.100 --> 01:07.400
What's it to you if we are?

01:08.050 --> 01:10.640
Well, I was talking with Ru—

01:10.640 --> 01:15.540
I want to try something with Shirakawa-san
 that's new for us both.

01:16.020 --> 01:16.720
Huh?

01:16.720 --> 01:20.020
So basically, I thought we could...

01:21.360 --> 01:24.020
Play survival games with girls?!

01:36.450 --> 01:43.080
<b>Our Dating Story: 
The Experienced You and The Inexperienced Me</b>

02:55.020 --> 02:57.740
<b>Our Survival Story:</b>

02:55.550 --> 02:57.740
<b>The Experienced You and the</b>

02:56.050 --> 02:57.740
<b>Inexperienced Us Play Survival Games.</b>

02:58.340 --> 02:59.960
Ta-da!

03:00.700 --> 03:02.910
Uh...

03:03.180 --> 03:04.870
Yay!

03:04.870 --> 03:06.090
<i>They're gyaru!</i>

03:09.040 --> 03:10.360
What a lovely smell.

03:15.710 --> 03:18.080
Okay! Ooh, the feels!

03:18.080 --> 03:21.180
Akari-champ, thank you very Machiko-sensei!

03:21.180 --> 03:23.130
Stahp!

03:23.640 --> 03:26.840
<i>I have absolutely no clue what they're saying.</i>

03:26.840 --> 03:27.850
<i>And also...</i>

03:27.850 --> 03:29.810
Runa, you're showing!

03:31.270 --> 03:32.270
Huh?

03:32.270 --> 03:34.980
No, I mean, it's dangerous 
to leave skin exposed.

03:34.980 --> 03:38.880
What? If a gyaru doesn't
 show skin, she'll die.

03:38.880 --> 03:40.950
Oh. Nishina-kun?

03:43.160 --> 03:45.580
We were in the same class last year.

03:45.580 --> 03:47.680
What class are you in now, Nishina-kun?

03:47.680 --> 03:48.490
Huh?!

03:49.120 --> 03:50.810
Ni-Ni-Nish...

03:53.160 --> 03:56.320
Ah, a girl called my name.

03:56.320 --> 03:58.050
And twice, at that.

03:58.050 --> 04:00.620
I feel you. I feel you, Nisshi.

04:00.620 --> 04:01.760
What's wrong?

04:01.760 --> 04:04.090
You guys seem kinda out of it today.

04:04.500 --> 04:05.970
The demon gyaru!

04:05.970 --> 04:08.560
You guys must be great at this stuff.

04:08.560 --> 04:10.230
I'm counting on you, okay?

04:10.680 --> 04:12.270
A-All right!

04:12.270 --> 04:14.440
The demon gyaru is the best!

04:14.440 --> 04:17.110
I'll take a bullet for the demon gyaru!

04:17.110 --> 04:18.550
Hey, Ryuto.

04:19.360 --> 04:21.640
Just watch me play today.

04:21.640 --> 04:25.410
I'm gonna get your heart with a critical hit!

04:25.410 --> 04:26.620
Bang!

04:30.290 --> 04:34.200
W-Weren't you just told that 
you shouldn't point that at people?

04:34.200 --> 04:37.500
Oh, you're right. Sorry!

04:37.500 --> 04:39.480
It's okay this time.

04:40.000 --> 04:43.090
<i>You've already shot through my heart anyway.</i>

04:43.090 --> 04:45.320
C-Curse you, Kasshi!

04:45.320 --> 04:47.930
Death to normies!

04:48.560 --> 04:51.890
Hold on. You mean I'm 
not good enough for you two?

04:52.740 --> 04:56.600
<i>Today's going to get complicated. 
In a lot of ways.</i>

05:01.860 --> 05:04.070
Game start!

05:04.070 --> 05:05.530
Normie, you're going down!

05:11.850 --> 05:12.890
Take cover!

05:13.620 --> 05:17.210
Ayy! I'll send you both straight to hell!

05:22.920 --> 05:23.800
Behind!

05:26.970 --> 05:28.720
Ow! Hit!

05:29.520 --> 05:31.050
<i>That's one down.</i>

05:34.890 --> 05:38.100
Nisshi, I will avenge you!

05:45.790 --> 05:47.660
Ryuto, you okay?

05:47.660 --> 05:50.200
I'm fine. Stay down, Runa.

05:52.160 --> 05:53.950
Eat this, Kasshi!

05:53.950 --> 05:55.870
Death to all normies!

05:58.800 --> 05:59.930
Hey!

06:03.710 --> 06:06.920
I missed him? Wah!

06:09.130 --> 06:10.330
Tanikita-san!

06:10.330 --> 06:12.100
Ah! Watch out, Akari!

06:15.220 --> 06:16.380
Ouch!

06:20.260 --> 06:21.730
Damn it. Hit!

06:22.030 --> 06:23.320
Take cover, quick!

06:23.320 --> 06:24.070
Mm-hmm.

06:30.990 --> 06:32.230
Hit.

06:33.480 --> 06:34.870
Ryuto...

06:34.870 --> 06:36.830
Aww, you got me!

06:37.160 --> 06:38.190
Akari...

06:38.990 --> 06:42.330
So you're the last one left, Runa.

06:42.790 --> 06:44.040
Nicole...

06:44.460 --> 06:48.010
You won't get me that easy! 
I'm fighting for Ryuto now too!

07:13.670 --> 07:14.950
Hit.

07:15.240 --> 07:16.500
Phew.

07:17.410 --> 07:22.750
Damn it. We couldn't sink the normies.

07:22.750 --> 07:25.660
Hey, Ryuto. Sorry about before.

07:25.660 --> 07:29.720
You were trying to protect me 
when you got shot, right?

07:29.720 --> 07:32.750
Uh, yeah. But it's totally fine.

07:32.750 --> 07:35.530
It would have been cooler 
if I had shot back, though.

07:35.530 --> 07:39.930
No, you were super cool! Thanks, Ryuto.

07:41.390 --> 07:43.530
Ack! Nicole! Your n-nails!

07:43.530 --> 07:46.440
Nice. Now it'll be easier to shoot.

07:46.440 --> 07:48.860
They kept getting stuck on the trigger.

07:50.980 --> 07:52.400
What? Hey!

07:52.820 --> 07:54.710
Let me borrow this for a bit.

07:56.220 --> 07:57.800
All right, all right, all right!

07:57.800 --> 08:00.080
Step up if you wanna get shot!

08:01.330 --> 08:02.800
Ahh! Hit!

08:02.800 --> 08:05.040
Nicole, you're too good at this!

08:05.040 --> 08:06.440
All right, all right, all right!

08:06.440 --> 08:08.130
Get rekt, noob punks!

08:08.690 --> 08:09.980
Ouch!

08:09.980 --> 08:12.340
The demon gyaru's bullet hit me!

08:12.340 --> 08:14.120
Wha—! Hit!

08:14.120 --> 08:16.800
I said you got me! Hit! Hit!

08:19.100 --> 08:20.720
Should we go, then?

08:21.760 --> 08:22.790
Oh, what?

08:23.500 --> 08:25.240
What's up, Runachi?

08:25.240 --> 08:29.660
My earring's gone. I know 
I put it in a case when we changed.

08:29.660 --> 08:32.480
Oh, the one with a moon and star?

08:32.480 --> 08:34.560
The one you always wear on one side?

08:34.560 --> 08:35.930
Yeah, that one.

08:35.930 --> 08:37.910
I know it means a lot to you.

08:37.910 --> 08:42.410
You even said you wouldn't wear it to school 
'cause you didn't want it to get confiscated.

08:42.410 --> 08:43.620
Yeah.

08:44.240 --> 08:46.250
Is it that important to you?

08:48.150 --> 08:49.550
Oh! Here it is!

08:51.510 --> 08:56.220
Sorry, it was buried in my bag. 
I guess it fell out of the case.

08:56.740 --> 08:59.610
I should've looked closer 
before I said anything.

08:59.610 --> 09:01.130
But at least you found it.

09:01.130 --> 09:01.930
Right?

09:01.930 --> 09:03.180
Okey-dokey.

09:03.640 --> 09:09.720
<i>I know I'm not into fashion, but how could I 
not have noticed Runa's special earring?</i>

09:10.150 --> 09:13.150
<i>And why does she only wear it on one side?</i>

09:14.320 --> 09:18.190
I still can't believe 
the demon gyaru won all by herself.

09:18.190 --> 09:21.400
Yeah, I guess the demon part isn't a joke.

09:24.500 --> 09:27.100
Wow, survival games sure were fun!

09:27.100 --> 09:28.250
You thought so?

09:28.250 --> 09:32.240
Yeah! The different types 
of airguns all shoot pellets differently.

09:32.240 --> 09:35.130
I bet it'd be fun to buy a bunch 
and try them out.

09:35.130 --> 09:39.050
I know, right? The airgun is 
the trigger for survival game fandom.

09:39.050 --> 09:41.790
I thought it was fun, too!

09:41.790 --> 09:44.140
It makes me want to try 
shooting all the different types.

09:44.140 --> 09:46.850
The ones we rented today 
were electric-powered guns, right?

09:44.220 --> 09:46.850
<b>The ones we rented today were electric-powered guns, right?</b>

09:46.690 --> 09:49.770
<b>They're fun 'cause you only have to pull a trigger to shoot,</b>

09:46.850 --> 09:49.180
They're fun 'cause you only have 
to pull a trigger to shoot,

09:49.020 --> 09:51.480
<b>but there are also gas guns and cocking air guns and stuff,</b>

09:49.180 --> 09:51.660
but there are also gas guns 
and cocking air guns and stuff,

09:51.150 --> 09:55.360
<b>and they all operate differently, so wouldn't
it be cool if you could master them all!</b>

09:51.660 --> 09:55.360
and they all operate differently, so wouldn't
it be cool if you could master them all?

09:55.360 --> 10:00.170
<i>Ah, Icchi... You've reverted
 to geeky rambling.</i>

10:00.570 --> 10:02.780
Huh. Is that right?

10:03.490 --> 10:04.790
<i>She kept up with him?!</i>

10:04.790 --> 10:08.970
Hmm. It does sound fun,
 but I'm a fan of too much stuff already.

10:08.970 --> 10:11.530
Akari's a pretty serious otaku,

10:11.530 --> 10:12.790
but I guess I am too.

10:12.790 --> 10:14.320
What? Really?

10:14.320 --> 10:15.420
An otaku for what?

10:15.840 --> 10:17.380
Vanilla Voice!

10:17.380 --> 10:20.140
Whenever they release a new CD, 
I buy multiple copies to get the bonus stuff.

10:17.380 --> 10:21.800
<b>Whenever they release a new CD, I buy multiple
 copies to get the bonus stuff. I get so deep into it!</b>

10:20.140 --> 10:21.610
I get so deep into it!

10:21.260 --> 10:24.060
<b>They're so cool, and their vibe is the bomb!</b>

10:21.610 --> 10:23.760
They're so cool, and their vibe is the bomb!

10:23.640 --> 10:25.850
<b>And they go all out for fan meets and signings!</b>

10:23.760 --> 10:25.850
And they go all out
 for fan meets and signings!

10:25.850 --> 10:28.170
And I'm a nail otaku.

10:28.170 --> 10:30.310
Right now, I'm into animal designs.

10:30.310 --> 10:32.350
Vivid croc designs are so great.

10:30.310 --> 10:33.150
<b>Vivid croc designs are so great.</b>

10:31.770 --> 10:35.110
<b>But swirl patterns might be coming back now, too.</b>

10:32.350 --> 10:34.590
But swirl patterns 
might be coming back now, too.

10:34.110 --> 10:36.940
<b>Water drops are still as popular as always.</b>

10:34.590 --> 10:36.560
Water drops are still as popular as always.

10:36.320 --> 10:39.070
<b>The gel and accessories are all cheap by themselves,</b>

10:36.560 --> 10:38.700
The gel and accessories 
are all cheap by themselves,

10:38.530 --> 10:41.280
<b>so before I knew it I bought too much and ran out of space!</b>

10:38.700 --> 10:41.280
so before I knew it I bought 
too much and ran out of space!

10:43.190 --> 10:44.540
What's wrong?

10:46.260 --> 10:49.960
It's so cool that you both 
have things you can get into.

10:49.960 --> 10:52.890
Well, you've got something too. 
Something you're into.

10:52.890 --> 10:53.660
Huh?

10:54.170 --> 10:55.130
Huh?

10:55.650 --> 10:59.090
You mean Ryuto? Oh, come on!

10:59.090 --> 11:03.550
I got an eyeful of you both today. 
It's honestly too much for a single girl.

11:04.010 --> 11:07.640
Hold it. Does that mean the demon 
gyaru doesn't have a boyfriend?

11:07.970 --> 11:11.680
I can't imagine dating anyone yet.

11:11.680 --> 11:14.120
Still can't forget your ex?

11:14.120 --> 11:17.660
Yeah. I mean, he was a really cool person.

11:17.660 --> 11:19.610
Cool? His looks?

11:19.610 --> 11:21.870
No, his attitude.

11:21.870 --> 11:26.350
He always had earphones in, 
and when I asked what he was listening to,

11:26.350 --> 11:28.580
he said "Buddhist sutras." 
Isn't that, like, crazy?

11:29.490 --> 11:31.640
That is definitely crazy.

11:31.640 --> 11:34.170
Talk about peak teenage angst.

11:34.170 --> 11:35.380
Huh?

11:36.840 --> 11:38.840
It sounds dumb, doesn't it?

11:38.840 --> 11:42.940
He's a boy I dated 
for just two weeks in eighth grade,

11:42.940 --> 11:45.300
and I still can't stop thinking about him.

11:45.300 --> 11:48.520
But he was the first person I really liked.

11:49.770 --> 11:52.270
Aww, Nicole.

11:52.270 --> 11:54.120
Two weeks...

11:54.120 --> 11:55.900
Does that mean she's still a vir—

11:56.480 --> 11:58.190
Ginouuuch!

11:59.280 --> 12:01.040
"Vir"? What was that?

12:01.040 --> 12:03.070
Are you begging for a virtuous death?

12:03.070 --> 12:05.490
Or you wanna get virtually flattened? Huh?

12:05.490 --> 12:07.720
Eeek! Never mind!

12:07.720 --> 12:09.820
Y-You okay, Nisshi?

12:09.820 --> 12:14.460
The pure demon gyaru gave me 
a wonderful reward. I am so grateful!

12:14.760 --> 12:17.920
I'd want to go out with someone who's tall.

12:17.920 --> 12:21.880
Huh? Someone tall? H-How tall?

12:21.880 --> 12:25.680
Hmm. I'm kinda small,
 so Jaemi might be too big,

12:25.680 --> 12:28.760
but someone about 
Jungwoo's size would be pretty cool.

12:28.760 --> 12:32.460
But hey, you're pretty tall too, 
Ijichi-kun. How tall are you?

12:32.460 --> 12:34.600
O-One hundred and eighty-one centimeters.

12:34.600 --> 12:36.990
What? That's the same as Lee Joon!

12:36.990 --> 12:38.440
So cool!

12:39.640 --> 12:43.710
<i>Lee Joon is, she means. 
But I get you. I get you, Icchi.</i>

12:43.710 --> 12:46.860
<i>A word like that feels like 
a royal medal to a geeky virgin!</i>

12:49.370 --> 12:52.590
Well, I gotta get to work.

12:52.590 --> 12:56.340
And I've got a livestream to watch, 
so I'm going home.

13:01.760 --> 13:03.580
I'm going home too.

13:03.580 --> 13:04.470
Me too.

13:08.890 --> 13:10.640
Wh-What about you?

13:10.640 --> 13:12.350
I'm still free.

13:12.350 --> 13:15.480
What do you want to do? Since we're 
already out, wanna go on a date?

13:15.480 --> 13:17.020
Y-Yeah, sure.

13:17.860 --> 13:20.460
There's a place I kinda want to go to.

13:32.700 --> 13:34.760
Yay! A Ferris wheel!

13:34.760 --> 13:36.670
I always wanted to ride one with you, Ryuto.

13:37.280 --> 13:39.130
O-Oh, really?

13:42.390 --> 13:45.130
<i>We're all alone in this small space...</i>

13:47.840 --> 13:49.850
We're so high up!

13:49.850 --> 13:50.790
Oh...

13:53.320 --> 13:55.870
W-We really are.

13:55.870 --> 13:58.190
<i>Ahh, I want to kiss her!</i>

13:58.190 --> 14:00.150
<i>Kiss! Kiss!</i>

14:00.150 --> 14:01.860
<i>Kiss, kiss, kiss!</i>

14:02.440 --> 14:03.800
<i>I want to kiss her!</i>

14:08.320 --> 14:11.280
I just remembered a
 shojo manga I used to read.

14:11.280 --> 14:12.640
A shojo manga?

14:12.640 --> 14:16.330
Yeah. It's one my mom used to have.

14:16.330 --> 14:20.190
The lead character and her boyfriend eat 
Marble Chocolates on a Ferris wheel together,

14:20.190 --> 14:22.570
and then they kiss.

14:22.570 --> 14:24.000
H-Huh.

14:24.000 --> 14:27.980
Then they say, "You taste like 
Marble Chocolates," and start laughing.

14:27.980 --> 14:32.970
I read it in elementary school and thought 
it was so mature. It was so exciting.

14:32.970 --> 14:35.930
I-I thought you weren't
 allowed to eat in here.

14:37.440 --> 14:40.020
Yeah, well, we don't have
 any chocolate anyway.

14:40.420 --> 14:42.770
But... can we?

14:45.010 --> 14:46.990
Y-Yeah.

15:10.120 --> 15:12.060
What did that taste like?

15:12.060 --> 15:12.640
Huh? Um...

15:12.640 --> 15:15.820
It smells like peaches.

15:15.820 --> 15:16.850
Bingo!

15:17.130 --> 15:21.310
I bought a new lip tint. 
It smells like peach tea. I love it!

15:21.310 --> 15:23.000
T-Tint?

15:23.000 --> 15:24.540
A kind of lip gloss.

15:24.540 --> 15:28.780
It didn't even stick to your lips. 
It's the good stuff!

15:29.510 --> 15:33.660
Yeah. You know, I really do like you, Ryuto.

15:34.320 --> 15:37.050
And I think I'll like you more and more.

15:40.000 --> 15:41.610
Hey, hey, Ryuto.

15:42.790 --> 15:44.670
Will you pat my head?

15:44.670 --> 15:46.330
Wh-Why?

15:46.330 --> 15:51.600
During the survival game, I wanted you
to say, "nice job," and pat me on the head.

15:51.600 --> 15:52.920
O-Okay.

15:52.920 --> 15:56.600
Yes! Okay, pat-pat me.

16:01.360 --> 16:02.980
Like that?

16:02.980 --> 16:05.110
Yeah, I love it!

16:09.650 --> 16:13.260
Thanks for inviting me out today. I had fun.

16:15.090 --> 16:16.160
Is something wrong?

16:16.620 --> 16:20.480
Uh-uh. I'm just so happy.

16:20.480 --> 16:25.870
We've been dating for two months, 
now it's almost three,

16:25.870 --> 16:29.000
and we're finally doing 
brand new things together.

16:29.000 --> 16:30.570
Oh, gosh. Sorry.

16:31.220 --> 16:33.510
I'm so happy, I might cry.

16:33.930 --> 16:35.600
Runa...

16:35.600 --> 16:38.000
What should we do 
for our three-month anniversary?

16:38.000 --> 16:41.060
It's a weekday, right? 
Is there something you want to do?

16:41.060 --> 16:42.300
Hmm.

16:43.600 --> 16:45.610
I think we've had enough anniversaries.

16:45.610 --> 16:46.400
Huh?

16:46.830 --> 16:50.360
As long as you're with me, Ryuto, 
that's all I need.

16:51.090 --> 16:55.820
Every day I can spend with you 
is so important to me.

16:55.820 --> 16:59.200
I started to realize that 
every day is a special day,

16:59.870 --> 17:02.070
so I think I've outgrown the anniversaries.

17:02.540 --> 17:03.630
Runa...

17:03.630 --> 17:06.160
I want to stay with you from here on too.

17:06.160 --> 17:08.720
I want us to keep smiling 
and growing into adults together!

17:08.720 --> 17:09.630
Yeah.

17:10.040 --> 17:11.520
You know what?

17:11.520 --> 17:15.090
I feel like I might be 
in love for the first time.

17:21.990 --> 17:23.820
<i>I want to keep up with you, Runa.</i>

17:29.010 --> 17:32.820
<i>No matter how far you run, 
I want to keep up with you!</i>

17:35.780 --> 17:40.310
<i>You're always looking 
toward our future together, and I...</i>

17:41.910 --> 17:44.700
<i>I want to become a man who's worthy of you!</i>

17:50.240 --> 17:53.130
<i>To make that happen, 
the only thing I can do now</i>

17:55.700 --> 17:57.860
<i>is study as hard as I can.</i>

17:59.080 --> 18:00.440
Hey, Ryuto.

18:02.090 --> 18:06.040
There's a cafe I want to go to 
on Saturday. Can we?

18:06.040 --> 18:08.510
Their croffles are really popular.

18:08.510 --> 18:10.650
Ah, sorry. It's Saturday.

18:10.650 --> 18:13.900
Oh, right. You have cram school.

18:13.900 --> 18:16.380
That's all right. Do your best!

18:18.640 --> 18:23.020
<i>And someday, I want to lose my virginity.</i>

18:28.610 --> 18:32.140
You know what? 
Yesterday, I tried making macarons.

18:32.140 --> 18:34.130
If you want, you can come over and try them.

18:34.900 --> 18:36.840
Huh? Wh-Why?!

18:40.880 --> 18:42.640
Maririn, let's sit by the windows.

18:42.640 --> 18:43.380
Yeah.

18:44.560 --> 18:46.220
Oh no! They're coming this way!

18:53.710 --> 18:54.360
Ouch!

18:56.720 --> 18:58.030
What just happened?

19:08.790 --> 19:11.630
Whoa, Yamada? Long time, man!

19:11.630 --> 19:15.080
Haven't seen you around, so I got worried.

19:16.000 --> 19:18.050
<b><i>Lunchtime Only</i></b>

19:16.000 --> 19:18.050
<b><i>Sandwich   Set</i></b>

19:18.130 --> 19:22.140
<b>Prep School ID

College Entrance Prep Course 
for High School Graduates


Sekiya Shugo


K Prep School Ikebukuro Campus</b>

19:18.130 --> 19:22.140
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

19:19.220 --> 19:22.140
Sekiya-san. Prep course 
for high school graduates?

19:22.430 --> 19:25.670
Yeah. I'm a ronin. Taking a gap year.

19:25.670 --> 19:28.400
Oh. But why do this?

19:28.400 --> 19:30.620
To rescue you.

19:30.620 --> 19:33.100
You were starting to look really suspicious.

19:33.620 --> 19:35.720
So, what's up with the girl?

19:35.720 --> 19:38.820
She your ex? A stalker? 
You can't let her see you?

19:39.280 --> 19:41.280
Huh? Uh, no...

19:41.580 --> 19:45.120
Ronin like me are starving 
for gossip like that.

19:45.120 --> 19:46.990
Why don't you tell me what's up?

19:47.510 --> 19:51.620
<i>I can't refuse right after 
he saved me from a big mess.</i>

19:52.040 --> 19:53.850
A-Actually...

19:57.070 --> 20:01.180
Huh. So the first girl who 
broke your heart turned out to be

20:01.180 --> 20:03.130
your current girlfriend's 
little sister, of all people.

20:03.540 --> 20:04.840
Yeah.

20:04.840 --> 20:09.980
So, what will you do? You gonna 
keep hiding until exams are over?

20:09.980 --> 20:14.660
I know it isn't very realistic, 
but I kind of have to.

20:14.660 --> 20:15.560
Why?

20:16.000 --> 20:20.150
I don't want to make my girlfriend worry.

20:20.840 --> 20:27.060
I made up my mind to stay away from that girl,
but now we're in the same cram school...

20:28.510 --> 20:32.730
I see what you mean. 
Then all you can do is hide for a while.

20:32.730 --> 20:34.370
Fine, I'll help you out.

20:34.650 --> 20:35.320
Huh?

20:35.320 --> 20:38.040
I'm at the Ikebukuro campus every day.

20:38.040 --> 20:40.730
If I spot that girl, 
I'll tell you where she is.

20:40.730 --> 20:42.080
Give me your ID.

20:42.080 --> 20:43.500
Oh. Okay.

20:43.500 --> 20:47.440
Anyway, I get that Kurose-san 
or whoever is a distraction,

20:47.440 --> 20:50.490
but at cram school, 
you really should focus on studying.

20:50.490 --> 20:51.340
Huh?

20:51.900 --> 20:56.980
There isn't a single good thing 
about being a ronin. Seriously.

20:57.480 --> 21:00.690
O-Oh. I'll work hard.

21:01.750 --> 21:06.610
All right. Let's hurry up and choose 
the committee for the culture festival.

21:06.610 --> 21:08.970
We have the sports festival in October,

21:06.610 --> 21:15.580
<b><i>Culture Festival Planning Committee</i></b>

21:08.970 --> 21:12.970
so we'll have to start planning 
November's culture festival at the same time.

21:12.970 --> 21:15.580
People who want to do it, 
please raise your hands.

21:18.540 --> 21:20.780
I can't do it. I'm too busy with club stuff.

21:20.780 --> 21:22.010
Me too.

21:22.010 --> 21:27.970
<b><i>Culture Festival Planning Committee</i></b>

21:23.540 --> 21:27.970
Come on, isn't there someone? 
I'm sure it'll be fun.

21:29.840 --> 21:30.860
Yes.

21:36.940 --> 21:38.900
Thank you, Kurose-san.

21:36.940 --> 21:38.900
<b><i>Kurose</i></b>

21:36.940 --> 21:38.900
<b><i>Culture Festival Planning Committee</i></b>

21:40.860 --> 21:42.380
Is there anyone else?

21:42.380 --> 21:43.570
Me! Me!

21:43.870 --> 21:45.780
I want to do it too!

21:50.200 --> 21:53.660
<i>The Friendship Project is finally launching!</i>

23:26.990 --> 23:28.510
On the next <i>Our Dating Story</i>,

23:28.880 --> 23:31.590
the experienced you and the inexperienced me

23:31.590 --> 23:33.760
start running together.

23:34.870 --> 23:38.020
Run, run! Runa for the win!

23:38.020 --> 23:40.020
<b>Our Running Story: The Experienced You and the Inexperienced Me Run Together.</b>
